---
/**
 * Hero and the single line of framing that precedes the questions.
 *
 * qs-2.0 deleted the scope panel: a six-row table explaining duration,
 * what you receive, what is assessed, what is not assessed, contact
 * details and answer handling, followed by a transmission statement and
 * a processing notice. Around two hundred words of explanation before a
 * single question, written to survive a review rather than to make
 * anyone curious.
 *
 * Almost all of it the interface communicates by itself. Duration is
 * obvious from a question counter. What you receive is obvious when you
 * receive it. What remains here is the two things that genuinely
 * prevent a misunderstanding, one of which is load-bearing legally:
 * nothing is assessed, and no contact details are needed.
 */
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="label reveal">Intervention Readiness Snapshot</span>
    <h1 class="h1 reveal">Can you stop it in time?</h1>
    <p class="lede muted reveal">
      You have governance. Controls. Named owners.
      Ten questions about one system that runs without you,
      and the last one is the one that matters.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row reveal">
      <a class="btn" href="#snapshot" data-snapshot-begin>Begin</a>
      <a class="btn-ghost" href="/sample-report/">See a tested verdict</a>
    </div>
    <p class="framing reveal">
      No sign-in and no contact details. Nothing here is assessed: it records
      what you tell it. Your answers stay in this tab until you press Generate.
      <a href="/legal/privacy/" class="link">Privacy</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-top: 144px;
    padding-bottom: 128px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }
  .hero .label { margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .hero .h1 { max-width: 14ch; }
  .hero .lede { margin-top: 32px; max-width: 40ch; }

  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 48px;
  }

  .framing {
    margin: 56px 0 0;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--faint);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .hero { padding-top: 112px; padding-bottom: 88px; }
  }
</style>
